```
Title: Potential HackTool - Defendnot Security Center AV Registry Modification
Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
Date: 2026-10-18
Level: medium
Description: Detects modification of the Microsoft Security Center AV registry keys, particularly those related with DisplayName, ProductEXE, or ReportingExe.
 These keys typically store information about antivirus products installed on the system, which is Windows Defender or third-party antivirus software.
 But, if these keys holds unexpected values or are modified in a suspicious manner, it could indicate an attempt to tamper with the security settings of the system.
MITRE Tactic: Uncategorized
Tags: attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1685
Reference: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_security_center_av_registry_modification.yml
 False Positives:
   - Legitimate changes by antivirus software missing in the filter list
```
TargetObject="*\\Software\\Microsoft\\Security Center\\Provider\\Av\\*" TargetObject IN ("*\\ProductEXE", "*\\DisplayName", "*\\ReportingExe") NOT (Details IN ("*Avira*", "*Windows Defender*", "*Microsoft Defender*", "*Sophos*", "*Kaspersky*", "*ESET*", "*Bitdefender*", "*Trend Micro*", "*McAfee*", "*Symantec*", "*CrowdStrike*", "*SentinelOne*", "*Carbon Black*", "*Elastic*", "*Cortex*", "*AVG*", "*Avast*", "*Malwarebytes*") Image="C:\\Windows\\System32\\svchost.exe")